  "dct_description_sm": [
    "<div>Bathymetry line data was collected to assess fish habitat in Ontario. Spot depths (bathymetry points) were used to measure the depth contours, which function like isobars to show lines of constant depth. Their density and positional accuracies vary depending on the survey style and parameters. This data should never be used for navigation.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Additional Documentation</strong></div><div><ul><li><a target='_blank' href='https://www.publicdocs.mnr.gov.on.ca/mirb/Bathymetry-UserGuide-EN.docx' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Bathymetry User Guide (Word)</a></li></ul></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Status</strong></div><div>On going: data is being continually updated</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Maintenance and Update Frequency</strong></div><div>As needed: data is updated as deemed necessary</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Contact</strong></div><div>Ontario Ministry of Natural Resources - Geospatial Ontario, <a href='mailto:geospatial@ontario.ca' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>geospatial@ontario.ca</a></div>"
